<dialog class="dialog" id="guide"><span class="over">Desk notes / 01</span><h2>Using the journal</h2><h3>Actual closes, not chart suggestions</h3><p>The Windows collector reads MT5 deal history. A partial exit is held until the remaining volume closes. Setups use the signal attached to the actual fills, not the number of legs the scanner planned. The two views are alternative units of analysis, never additive.</p><h3>Connect or import</h3><p>With the kit extracted on the MT5 computer, run <code>py -3 journal.py</code>, then open <code>http://127.0.0.1:8765</code>. To enrich the journal with bot receipts and structure types, add <code>--repo "path to bot"</code>. For automatic session columns on Windows, install <code>tzdata</code> in that same Python environment if not present. The full Windows steps are in <code>START-HERE.md</code>.</p><p>This HTML also works offline. Import <code>tickets.csv</code>, <code>setups.csv</code> or select both together. An import replaces the current dataset; a ticket file alone cannot prove that a setup is complete. No uploaded files leave the browser.</p><h3>Optional local demo controls</h3><p>Only the Windows collector opened with <code>Start-Journal-Demo-Controls.cmd</code> exposes the launch panel. Run the read-only checks, review the exact enabled private YAML profiles, then type <code>ARM DEMO</code> to explicitly authorize starting a separate order-capable demo scanner. Opening this page or importing a CSV cannot arm it.</p><h3>Read the numbers</h3><p>Net = deal profit + signed commission + swap + fees, including entry costs. Win rate is wins ÷ all closed records, including breakevens. Filters and both charts use the selected unit and close dates. The curve starts at zero for your selection; it is not account equity. CSV times are always UTC; EAT is UTC+3.</p><h3>Reasons, gross P/L and sessions</h3><p>The entry reason is the recorded qualifying market-structure setup. Missing evidence is shown as <strong>Not recorded</strong>, never reconstructed from P/L. The exit reason is from the final broker exit deal; a generic Hull exit does not prove an opposite-signal exit. When the audit contains a unique successful nearby request for the same ticket, its reason is shown separately (for example, opposite Hull label). It is not inferred from an SL or TP. Setups with different ticket exits show Mixed exits.</p><p>Gross P/L is signed broker deal profit before commission, swap and fees. Gross gains/losses show positive/negative record contributions separately. Switch Tickets / Setups to change the unit of analysis.</p><p>Session buckets use the selected entry or exit timestamp. Analytical FX windows, Monday–Friday in each city: Sydney 08:00–17:00, Tokyo 09:00–18:00, London 08:00–17:00, New York 08:00–17:00. City daylight-saving rules apply. Overlaps get one combined bucket; Off-session is retained. These are not instrument-specific exchange hours or a holiday calendar.</p><p id="diagnostics" class="infoLine"></p><div class="actions"><button class="btn primary" data-close="guide">Done</button></div></dialog>
